es equity and fixed income mutual funds. The firm invests in the public equity and fixed income markets across the globe. It employs fundamental and quantitative analysis with a bottom-up approach. The firm utilizes in-house and external research to make its investments. It employs socially responsible investing with a focus on environmental, social, and governance issues. It makes investment in late-stage venture capital transactions and usually invests between $3 million and $5 million. The firm was previously known as T. Rowe Group, Inc. and T. Rowe Price Associates, Inc. T. Rowe Price Group, Inc. was founded in 1937 and is based in Baltimore, Maryland, with additional offices in North America, Europe, Asia, Australia.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Robert W. Sharps C.F.A., CPA | CEO & Chair of the Board | Age 54 | Compensation: $8.8M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 7K people. Revenue per employee of $957K ranks in the above the sector median among Financial Services peers, with revenue growing 9%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $194K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $28K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 9\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["T. Rowe Price Group, Inc. is a large-cap financial services business with a $23.2B market cap on $7.3B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +4% over the past three years, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 23% against a 11% cost of capital \u2014 a 12-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat. Gross margins of 100% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $1.5B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 20 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, with adequate 0.84\u00d7 cash conversion.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 7.6% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 2/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Price sits 28% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.2791003081037252},{"text":"Elevated short interest (14.8% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Financial Services peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Valued at a 34% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","39 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Gross margin tops the Financial Services peer set \u2014 genuine pricing power is present here"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Is T. Rowe Price Mid-Cap Value (TRMCX) a Strong Mutual Fund Pick Right Now?","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/t-rowe-price-mid-cap-110002295.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794567602.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.691,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Joel Isaacson & Co. LLC Buys New Holdings in T. Rowe Price Technology ETF $TTEQ","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/joel-isaacson-co-llc-buys-new-holdings-in-t-rowe-price-technology-etf-tteq.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794565665.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.896,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"T. Rowe Price Blue Chip Growth ETF $TCHP Stock Bought by Kestra Advisory Services LLC","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/t-rowe-price-blue-chip-growth-etf-tchp-stock-bought-by-kestra-advisory-services-llc.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794563237.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.919,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"T. Rowe Price October AUM Falls 1.6% Sequentially Amid Net Outflows","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3028993/t-rowe-price-october-aum-falls-1-6-sequentially-amid-net-outflows?cid=CS-ZC-FT-analyst_blog%7Ccompany_news_finance_sector-3028993","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794504120.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Treasury Secretary Scott Bessent Disclosed His Entire 401(k) Is In A Single T. Rowe Price Fund. Here\u2019s Who T. Rowe Price Says It\u2019s Built For","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/treasury-secretary-scott-bessent-disclosed-151620000.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794496824.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.103,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"BlackRock's Private Markets Expansion: A Key Long-Term Growth Driver?","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stock